# Top-level ignores. The platform directories carry their own, narrower rules
# (android/.gitignore for Gradle + the gomobile .aar, ios/.gitignore for the
# xcframework, the xcodegen-generated project and Xcode build state), so this
# file deliberately covers only what those two don't: Go build output, the
# artifacts the examples and the WASM target write into the tree, and editor
# or OS cruft.

# Go build and test output. Binaries land next to their package when built
# without -o, so ignore the compiled test binaries and coverage profiles
# rather than trying to enumerate example binary names.
*.test
*.out
*.exe
coverage.html

# The two binaries a bare `go build` leaves in the tree that were once
# committed: `go build ./examples/chat` from the root writes ./chat, and the
# docs server built in its own module directory writes cmd/docs/docs. Both
# were tracked (a fifth of every module download) until plan Part D item 1.
# internal/trackedfiles now fails on any tracked compiled program by content,
# so these lines only stop `git add -A` from offering them again.
/chat
/cmd/docs/docs

# WASM target. index.html fetches main.wasm from this directory; it is a build
# product of `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build -o wasm/main.wasm ./wasm`.
# wasm_exec.js is NOT ignored — it is copied from the Go toolchain and tracked
# so the page works without a local Go install.
wasm/main.wasm
# build.sh's precompressed copies of the page's files (serve sends them to
# browsers that accept them), and the .tmp each is written through.
wasm/*.gz
wasm/*.br
wasm/*.tmp

# htmlout demo output. Several examples render to a static page in the working
# directory (examples/chat -> social.html, examples/layout -> layout.html,
# examples/fintechapp -> materialwallet.html); these are regenerated by running
# the example, never committed.
social.html
layout.html
materialwallet.html

# Local scratch: agent/tool state that is per-checkout, not per-project.
.cats-todo/

# Claude Code. .claude/ itself IS tracked — .claude/commands/ holds this
# repository's own slash commands, which are as much a part of how it is worked
# on as build.sh is. What is not tracked is the settings a person accumulates
# in their own checkout: settings.local.json is where permission grants land as
# they are approved, so it differs per machine and per person and would
# conflict on every pull.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.ced/
.vscode/
*.swp

# The ARIA specification, fetched by aria/fetch.sh for aria/gen and
# aria/verify. Not committed: see aria/fetch.sh for why.
aria/spec/testdata/
